.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
data/
*.db
*.sqlite*
.env

# models/ is deliberately NOT excluded, because `MODEL_DIR` in
# docker-compose.offline.yml points the running backend at /app/models and the
# Dockerfile COPYs it there. Without the artefacts the image builds clean,
# starts clean, and reports every model-backed attribute as UNAVAILABLE with a
# reason — `track_b/service.py` degrades rather than fails, by design — so a
# missing model directory is invisible from outside. MT-26 opens the image and
# looks.
#
# `*.pt` stays excluded, and it is the one exclusion here that is a decision
# rather than housekeeping. `traffic_cnn.pt` is the CNN, and inference
# deliberately loads the LightGBM booster instead: loading the CNN would make
# torch a runtime dependency of the API and of this image, for a model whose
# scores `models/metrics.json` already records. It is gitignored for the same
# reason, so a clean clone does not have it either. Nothing at run time reads
# it.
models/*.pt
models/*.pkl
models/*.joblib
models/*.onnx
